        "title": "Why does evidence often confirm what we already believe? Confirmation bias",
        "lead": "Two readers can look at the same news story and draw completely different conclusions. The problem involves how we select, interpret and check information as well as which information we find. Confirmation bias shows why a good question often matters more than ten further examples that flatter our initial idea.",
